{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "23", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "14", "M": "29", "S": "47"}}, "news": [{"title": "Shriram Properties to pump in \u20b94,000 crore more into Uttarpara project", "para": "Shriram Properties plans a massive investment of Rs 4,000 crore in its Uttarpara project, diversifying into residential, commercial, healthcare, and educational facilities. Having already invested Rs 2,000 crore, they've developed 65 acres, with ongoing projects including 3,400 flats in phase two and 198 villas in phase three. The company's CMD envisions a transformation that will turn Uttarpara into a thriving hub akin to Bengaluru's Whitefield.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/shriram-properties-to-pump-in-4000-crore-more-into-uttarpara-project/134439833?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-475572/134439833.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Runwal Enterprises targets 2:1 debt-equity ratio after IPO: Chairman", "para": "Runwal Enterprises is gearing up for a significant Rs 500-crore initial public offering set to debut on September 25. The funds raised will facilitate debt repayment and support new project acquisitions. With a current debt-to-equity ratio of 3:1, the company aims to trim this down to 2:1. Furthermore, it plans to transition to an asset-light model and focus on expansion in the western suburbs over the next few years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/runwal-enterprises-targets-21-debt-equity-ratio-after-ipo-chairman/134437953?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-65934/134437953.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Kotak Alts raises \u20b95,000 crore for private credit, real assets fund", "para": "Kotak Alternate Asset Managers has announced the final close of its Kotak Yield & Growth Fund at \u20b95,000 crore, raised entirely from domestic investors. The Category II AIF had achieved a first close of \u20b93,900 crore in February 2026.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/kotak-alts-raises-5000-crore-for-private-credit-real-assets-fund/134435038?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-57304/134435038.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}